    "qualifierLines": [
      "{**42 NY3d at 371} OPINION OF THE COURT",
      "The Appellate Division affirmed with one Justice dissenting (214 AD3d 1428 [4th Dept 2023]). The sole issue dividing the Court was defendant's claim that he was denied his right to be present during consideration of the prosecution's Sandoval application. The majority concluded that defendant had not been denied this right. The dissent concluded that defendant, although present for the later Sandoval proceeding, was denied an opportunity to meaningfully participate (see id. at 1429 [Curran, J., dissenting]). The dissenting Justice granted defendant leave to appeal."
